+5.  **Variance Loss:** To decrease ambiguity in low-texture areas, the variance of the predicted density distribution and color values along each ray is regularized. This comprises two terms, $L_w^{var}(\mathbf{r})$ and $L_{var}(\mathbf{r})$ (Eqs. 5 and 6 in [S1]). [G] *Implementer Note: The text states these constrain density and color distribution. Typically, this involves minimizing the variance of the weights $w(t)$ and the color values $\mathbf{c}(t)$ along the ray to force a single dominant surface interaction rather than a diffuse spread. The exact formulas for Eqs. 5 and 6 are not provided in the source text.*
 
